# Laravel Modular Monolith Layering

## Module Layout

Each domain under `app/Modules/<Module>/` owns:

`Controllers/`, `Requests/`, `Services/`, `Repositories/`, `Interfaces/`, `Models/`, `Policies/`

Mirror an existing module before scaffolding. Register interface→repository bindings and policies in `app/Providers/RepositoryServiceProvider.php`.

## Required Flow

```text
HTTP → Controller → FormRequest → Service → RepositoryInterface → Repository → Model → DB
```

| Layer | Does | Must Not |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Controller | `$this->authorize()`, call service, return view/redirect | Query models, business logic, branch rules |
| FormRequest | Validation rules, input normalization | Domain ownership as sole protection, DB writes |
| Service | Business rules, BranchContext, transactions | Render views, bypass repositories |
| Repository | Query, filter, paginate, persist | Authorization, workflow decisions |
| Policy | Permission/role/branch checks | Heavy queries, persistence, workflows |
| Model | Fillable, casts, relations, scopes | Workflow orchestration, auth decisions |

## Scaffolding Order

1. Read existing module conventions
2. Model + migration (only if explicitly requested)
3. Interface + Repository
4. Service (inject interface, use transactions)
5. FormRequests (one per write action)
6. Policy
7. Thin Controller
8. Wire bindings, policies, routes
9. Pest feature tests (validation, auth, happy path, branch isolation)
10. Run Pint + tests

## Valid Controller Pattern

```php
public function store(StoreProductRequest $request): RedirectResponse
{
    $this->authorize('create', Product::class);
    $product = $this->products->create($request->validated());
    return redirect()->route('inventory.products.show', $product)
        ->with('status', 'Product created.');
}
```

## Forbidden Patterns

- `Product::create($request->all())` in controllers
- Concrete repository injection when interface exists
- Business logic in Blade or repositories
- Unscoped `Model::findOrFail($id)` for branch-owned records

## Testing

Use Pest with `RefreshDatabase`. Prove allowed and denied paths. Branch isolation tests are mandatory for branch-owned features.
